    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d114">

                <pb facs="0700" n="673" xml:id="pg673"/>

                <head>114. Memorandum From Jeffrey Starr of
                    the Delegation to the Nuclear and Space Talks in Geneva to the Arms Control and
                    Disarmament Agency (Lehman)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d114-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Geneva</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1990-05-09">May 9, 1990</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Outstanding START Issues</item>
                </list>
                <p>As requested, attached is the list of 32 issues which the Secretary and the
                    Soviet Foreign Minister agreed in April to attempt to resolve in Geneva before
                    the next ministerial. You should be aware also that Ambassadors Burt and Nazarkin have agreed to expand the 32 issues list to 50 issues.
                    The Delegation has drawn up a list of additional issues and will begin
                    discussions with the Soviets tomorrow on it. There is no formal list of issues,
                    internal or agreed, to be resolved by the time of the summit; in fact, there has
                    been some reluctance to draw up such a list. Nonetheless, a list of other
                    outstanding START issues is attached.</p>




                <xi:include href="d114-a1.xml" xpointer="d114-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d114-a2.xml" xpointer="d114-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
